Hi Nicolas and Colby,

sorry about the delay here.  Obviously something is not correct when
aroma.affymetrix only has four(!) positive values to calculate the
target distribution.

Right now I'm suspecting that the numbers for one of the arrays might
have failed.  Let's try to troubleshoot that first, and then I'll try
to add more exception handling to catch such errors/issues:

First, see if there is any odd results from the average.  What does
the following output?

ces <- getChipEffectSet(plm);
ceR <- getAverageFile(ces);
thetaR <- extractMatrix(ceR);
print(summary(log2(thetaR)));

If there are a lot of NAs in the log-chip effects, we're onto something.

Then, let's calculate some "boxplot" statistics of the log-chip
effects for each array (this may take some time):

stats <- boxplotStats(ces, type="theta", transform=log2, verbose=-5)
str(stats);

You should see something like:

List of 96
 $ NA06985:List of 4
  ..$ stats: num [1:5]  9.6 11.5 12.2 12.8 14.7
  ..$ n    : int 1881322
  ..$ conf : num [1:2] 12.2 12.2
  ..$ out  : num [1:25127] 8.52 9.18 8.98 8.29 9.42 ...
[...]
$ NA07019:List of 4
 ..$ stats: num [1:5]  9.56 11.49 12.16 12.77 14.70
 ..$ n    : int 1881362
 ..$ conf : num [1:2] 12.2 12.2
 ..$ out  : num [1:24063] 8.82 9.39 8.52 9.22 8.78 ...
- attr(*, "type")= chr "theta"
- attr(*, "transform")=function (x)

Does any of the arrays "look odd" to you?  The 'n' value indicates the
number of non-missing values after the log-transform.

Cheers

Henrik

