Hi,

On Thu, May 8, 2008 at 1:27 PM, Matt <matt.k...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>  Thanks. It works now but only when I omit the arguments combineAlleles
>  and mergeStrands. I checked my plm model and I did indeed set these at
>  TRUE. Here's what happens when I use these arguments:
>
>
>  > name <- "HapMap_CEU";
>  > tags <- c("ACC", "-XY", "RMA", "A+B", "FLN", "-XY");
>  > chipType <- "Mapping250K_Nsp";
>  > ces <- ChipEffectSet$fromName(name, tags=tags, chipType=chipType,
>  + combineAlleles=TRUE, mergeStrands=TRUE)
>  Error in list("ChipEffectSet$fromName(name, tags = tags, chipType =
>  chipType, combineAllel" = <environment>,  :
>
>  [2008-05-08 15:48:05] Exception: Unknown arguments: combineAlleles,
>  mergeStrands
>   at throw(Exception(...))
>
>   at throw.default("Unknown arguments: ", argsStr)
>   at throw("Unknown arguments: ", argsStr)
>   at AffymetrixFileSet(files = files, ...)
>   at extend(AffymetrixFileSet(files = files, ...), "AffymetrixCelSet",
>  "cached:.
>   at AffymetrixCelSet(...)
>   at extend(AffymetrixCelSet(...), "ParameterCelSet")
>   at ParameterCelSet(...)
>   at extend(ParameterCelSet(...), "ChipEffectSet",
>  "cached:.firstCells" = NULL,
>
>   at this(...)
>   at newInstance.Class(clazz, ...)
>   at newInstance(clazz, ...)
>   at newInstance.Object(static, files, ...)
>   at newInstance(static, files, ...)
>   at fromFiles.GenericDataFileSet(static, ..., fileClass = fileClass)
>   at fromFiles.AffymetrixFileSet(static, path = path, pattern =
>  pattern, ..., fi
>   at fromFiles.AffymetrixCelSet(static, path = path, pattern =
>  pattern, ..., fil
>
>   at method(this, ...)
>   at static$fromFiles(path = path, cdf = cdf, ...)
>   at with

yet another jet-lag typo by me.  The class ChipEffectSet does not know
about 'mergeStrands' and 'combineAlleles', but CnChipEffectSet does.
Thus, do:

 ces <- CnChipEffectSet$fromName(name, tags=tags, chipType=chipType,
                                                 combineAlleles=TRUE,
mergeStrands=TRUE);

Note the class.

Also, I've committed more patches so download those first;

library(aroma.affymetrix);
downloadPackagePatch("aroma.affymetrix");

/Henrik

>
>
>
> On May 8, 1:33 pm, "Henrik Bengtsson" <h...@stat.berkeley.edu> wrote:
>  > Hi.
>  >
>
>
> > On Thu, May 8, 2008 at 10:02 AM, Elizabeth Purdom <epur...@gmail.com> wrote:
>  >
>  > >  Henrik Bengtsson wrote:
>  > >  > Note that there is in neither case a path specified; this works
>  > >  > because the code searches both rawData/ and plmData/ for the data set.
>  > >  >  This is exactly how you defined your the first CEL set.
>  > >  Hi Henrik,
>  > >  The reason I put in the path="plmData" in my response is because I
>  > >  thought the default search directories for 'findByName' (which finds the
>  > >  path directory) were c("rawData","probeData") and NOT 'plmData'; I don't
>  > >  see that byName() changes these options. So wouldn't you have to specify
>  > >  the path?
>  >
>  > See my most recent reply to Mark.  What is going on is that there is
>  > one byName() (alias findName()) common for all AffymetrixCelSet
>  > classes, which in turn calls findByName() which is specific to each
>  > subclass, e.g.
>  >
>  > > args(findByName.AffymetrixCelSet)
>  >
>  > function (static, name, tags=NULL, chipType=NULL, paths=c("rawData",
>  > "probeData"), ...)
>  > NULL> args(findByName.ChipEffectSet)
>  >
>  > function (static, ..., paths="plmData/")
>  > NULL
>  >
>  > Cheers
>  >
>  > /Henrik
>  >
>  > >  Best,
>  > >  Elizabeth
>  >
