> example, in the code chunk below you will see that I can only derive
> 262,217 total SNPs and only 5705 on chromosome X on which there should
> be 5710 (based on what I found using another package for SNP chip
> data).

In any case, the genome information is retrieved from the UGP file,
whose information is imported from the public Affymetrix NetAffx CSV
file.  The Mapping250K_Nsp,na24,HB20080214.ugp file is from NetAffx
release 24 (hence tag 'na24').  That is the source of your statistics.
 I don't have a specific documentation on how to build the UGP for
this chip type, but Page 'Building UGP and UFL files for the 100K chip
set' [http://groups.google.com/group/aroma-affymetrix/web/mapping50k-hind240-mapping50k-xba240---creating-ugp-and-ufl-files]
give you the idea.  It is on my todo list to build UGP files for
NetAffx release 25 - then you might get different numbers.

..."another package for SNP chip data" is quite a vague statement -
whose "correct"?!?

Cheers

Henrik

